  "Delib_end_time": "11:33 a.m.",
  "notes": "Deliberations had concluded before court convened; court opened at 11:33 a.m. specifically to receive the verdict. Deliberation start time not recorded in this document — likely in a prior day's minutes. Total time in court was only 10 minutes. Jury verdict filed conventionally per General Order 2007-3."
}

{
  "Final_trial_day": 4,
  "Delib_start_time": "10:33 a.m.",
  "Delib_end_time": "2:34 p.m.",
  "notes": "The verdict notification timestamp is recorded as '2:10 a.m.' which is almost certainly a typographical error and should read '2:10 p.m.' given the sequential context of the day's events. Multiple Court Security Officers were sworn in at intervals during deliberations (Gary Osborne at 11:00 a.m., Katherine Maestas at 11:30 a.m., Terry Simmons at 12:30 p.m.). Jurors were polled at the request of the defendant."
}

{
  "Delib_start_time": "1:30 p.m.",
  "Delib_adjourn_time": "4:32 p.m.",
  "Delib_resume_time": null,
  "notes": "Jury submitted a question at 2:40 p.m. during deliberations; court recessed to research the answer and delivered it to the jury at 3:06 p.m. Jury had not reached a verdict by end of day and was excused until 9:00 a.m. on May 22, 2015. Court also advised jury of Rule 50 rulings dismissing Defendant Ensminger and finding Defendants Weatherill's and Hartbauer's violation of Plaintiff's 4th Amendment rights before deliberations began."
}

{
  "Final_trial_day": 5,
